    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d655">

                <pb facs="0848" n="836" xml:id="pg836"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.67/8–1246: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Durbrow</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-08-12T15:00:00+03:00">August 12, 1946—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 12—1:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3159. Understand that during his recent conversation with Masaryk<anchor n="57"
                        xml:id="d655-f1"/> and other Czechs Stalin gratuitously and out of context
                    stated three times that USSR had no intention of attacking Turkey.</p>
                <p>Sent to Ankara as 43.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Durbrow</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d655-f1" n="57" xml:id="d655-f1-content">
                <p>Jan Masaryk, Czechoslovak Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
